cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Predicting Winter Wheat Yield Across German Federal States with DWD Climate Data"
authors:
  - given-names: Shahid
    family-names: Nawaz
repository-code: "https://github.com/mshahid888/project-03-winter-wheat-yield-forecasting"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Forecasting Bundesland-level winter-wheat yield in Germany from the previous year's yield
  and pre-harvest DWD climate aggregates, using a chronological 2020-2025 holdout and a
  persistence baseline. Neither Ridge regression nor the tested Random Forest configuration
  improves on the persistence baseline on the holdout. Significance tests reported in the
  documentation, run outside this repository and not reproducible from its code, indicate
  the differences are within noise.
keywords:
  - "yield forecasting"
  - "winter wheat"
  - "Germany"
  - "DWD"
  - "machine learning"
  - "time series"
  - "scikit-learn"
